        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "63cf89ce-0470-3e9f-b1e5-453d7aa67d1e",
                "word": "вброд",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a0cb4624-c2cc-31a9-8d97-0eed6ec24b51",
                        "entry_id": "63cf89ce-0470-3e9f-b1e5-453d7aa67d1e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "бредя, переходя водоём по дну в неглубоком месте"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "с глаголами движения"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4153b9d8-a1db-4357-8a9b-582c986dd75c",
                                "sense_id": "a0cb4624-c2cc-31a9-8d97-0eed6ec24b51",
                                "text": "Обозначеннный мост, где насыпной тракт пересекает Пайпудыну не существует. Грузовики колесят её в том месте вброд. Вброд речка проходится легко."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfb3bc7c-b180-47c7-bce8-77706d04fea8",
                                "sense_id": "a0cb4624-c2cc-31a9-8d97-0eed6ec24b51",
                                "text": "Несмотря на то, что казаки каждый час ожидали переправы и нападения абреков с татарской стороны, особенно в мае месяце, когда лес по Тереку так густ, что пешему трудно пролезть чрез него, а река так мелка, что кое-где можно переезжать её вброд, и несмотря на то, что дня два тому назад прибегал от полкового командира казак с цидулкой в которой значилось, что, по полученным чрез лазутчиков сведениям, партия в восемь человек намерена переправиться через Терек, и потому предписывается наблюдать особую осторожность, — на кордоне не соблюдалось особенной осторожности."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "587c3309-097a-4872-9a41-961114f7a28c",
                        "source_entry_id": "63cf89ce-0470-3e9f-b1e5-453d7aa67d1e",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0cb4624-c2cc-31a9-8d97-0eed6ec24b51",
                        "target_lang_word": "wade",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wade",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d4e8403-cf14-31ba-8f44-a60de3eb57fb",
                                        "entry_id": "47e3d3da-2252-34b1-afa4-699898eeb8f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To walk through water or something that impedes progress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3eb5f3d-5eef-49a3-abc1-c5af488971f3",
                                                "sense_id": "9d4e8403-cf14-31ba-8f44-a60de3eb57fb",
                                                "text": "So eagerly the fiend […] / With head, hands, wings, or feet, pursues his way, / And swims, or sinks, or wades, or creeps, or flies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c6a6ef4-7652-4830-be3a-9ee24d678138",
                                                "sense_id": "9d4e8403-cf14-31ba-8f44-a60de3eb57fb",
                                                "text": "After breakfast the men set out to hunt, while the women went to a large pool of warm water covered with a green scum and filled with billions of tadpoles. They waded in to where the water was about a foot deep and lay down in the mud. They remained there from one to two hours and then returned to the cliff."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0da12d7b-7525-34c9-b49a-1e8e71d45ef5",
                                        "entry_id": "47e3d3da-2252-34b1-afa4-699898eeb8f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To progress with difficulty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e397f8e-be96-4bfd-8793-2904502f4aa5",
                                                "sense_id": "0da12d7b-7525-34c9-b49a-1e8e71d45ef5",
                                                "text": "to wade through a dull book"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dab8f980-b40f-480e-8829-6eb51c3e3b29",
                                                "sense_id": "0da12d7b-7525-34c9-b49a-1e8e71d45ef5",
                                                "text": "And wades through fumes, and gropes his way."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8041fff2-7ee2-4ce4-a4da-f4c111b7e8b6",
                                                "sense_id": "0da12d7b-7525-34c9-b49a-1e8e71d45ef5",
                                                "text": "The king's admirable conduct has waded through all these difficulties."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eec4f70f-63fd-3fc4-94ea-726e35a01f20",
                                        "entry_id": "47e3d3da-2252-34b1-afa4-699898eeb8f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To walk through (water or similar impediment); to pass through by wading."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "185f3d86-7fe7-4033-aafd-69a6c8d4825a",
                                                "sense_id": "eec4f70f-63fd-3fc4-94ea-726e35a01f20",
                                                "text": "wading swamps and rivers"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45f86902-f656-3f50-afa5-a5087053d788",
                                        "entry_id": "47e3d3da-2252-34b1-afa4-699898eeb8f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To gleam intermittently through clouds or mist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of the sun or moon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29117734-5267-4e02-a16e-f2b8bcdadc8f",
                                                "sense_id": "45f86902-f656-3f50-afa5-a5087053d788",
                                                "text": "I saw my Meg come linking o'er the lee; I saw my Meg, but Maggy saw nae me: For yet the sun was wading through the mist, And she was close upon me ere she wist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44e3e09b-297a-405e-a7d7-ac7d71faa200",
                                                "sense_id": "45f86902-f656-3f50-afa5-a5087053d788",
                                                "text": "... the pale light of a crescent moon wading among the black and lowering clouds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0bd869a-b5b6-4cbd-b96c-0758834b795d",
                                                "sense_id": "45f86902-f656-3f50-afa5-a5087053d788",
                                                "text": "When sunshine has a scorching and enervating effect on man, during the greater part of the day, the next day will be cloudy and perhaps rainy. When the sun wades through clouds of any kind, rain may or may not follow;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e86b13a2-1db6-47da-baf5-a5e1228b8a96",
                                                "sense_id": "45f86902-f656-3f50-afa5-a5087053d788",
                                                "text": "[…] the sun is \"wading\" when it is struggling through a heavy scud, and the moon is \"sitting\" when her dark side is turned towards the earth. The poets themselves may be in vain searched for a finer expression than the first."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e93ca4b-754b-4179-95b6-9a471564b03a",
                                                "sense_id": "45f86902-f656-3f50-afa5-a5087053d788",
                                                "text": "The moon, which had arisen during their conversation, was, in the phrase of that country, wading or struggling with clouds, and shed only a doubtful and occasional light."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfc53234-4b6d-4100-9562-6a03ed44da10",
                                                "sense_id": "45f86902-f656-3f50-afa5-a5087053d788",
                                                "text": "It's rain afoor meeght, t'sun waded sadly ez sha peeped ower Roseberry."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c15e005c-3a06-3fdd-8453-c62b79fc8459",
                                        "entry_id": "47e3d3da-2252-34b1-afa4-699898eeb8f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To enter recklessly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1716f49-e07f-4074-98e6-a01c46d45f9b",
                                                "sense_id": "c15e005c-3a06-3fdd-8453-c62b79fc8459",
                                                "text": "to wade into a fight or a debate"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "334f7aff-337c-4980-b1a7-24bce210df99",
                                                "sense_id": "c15e005c-3a06-3fdd-8453-c62b79fc8459",
                                                "text": "Thailand’s Queen Mother Sirikit, who brought glamour to a postwar revival in the country’s monarchy and who, in later years, would occasionally wade into politics, has died aged 93 […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wade",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34be3d00-2435-3c9e-929e-c203d6c29497",
                                        "entry_id": "e4dae90e-42f7-3ac9-ad7e-4f63d1c608b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of wading."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec5b2d9b-4c9e-4ee8-a40d-1eef1e010e83",
                                                "sense_id": "34be3d00-2435-3c9e-929e-c203d6c29497",
                                                "text": "We had to be careful during our dangerous wade across the river."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1fb8e9b-7530-31f9-9075-f366b57e5628",
                                        "entry_id": "e4dae90e-42f7-3ac9-ad7e-4f63d1c608b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ford; a place to cross a river."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wade",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e557a978-6675-3ffa-938a-af8cbd4fc43c",
                                        "entry_id": "a8ddd2b2-50f6-38b8-b53c-f7b6e02cfc63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Obsolete form of woad."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90684ee6-4332-43c3-8e4c-0feced30cf5c",
                                                "sense_id": "e557a978-6675-3ffa-938a-af8cbd4fc43c",
                                                "text": "Woad or Wade is a very rich Commodity"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "91849f0d-53d8-477a-b28f-927c3c6b99fe",
                        "source_entry_id": "63cf89ce-0470-3e9f-b1e5-453d7aa67d1e",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0cb4624-c2cc-31a9-8d97-0eed6ec24b51",
                        "target_lang_word": "ford",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ford",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1720e38d-4a85-36ac-bd53-0f39d4c684b5",
                                        "entry_id": "8003c089-83ad-3b87-a687-c807b7e55044",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A location where a stream is shallow and the bottom has good footing, making it possible to cross from one side to the other with no bridge, by walking, riding, or driving through the water; a crossing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31336216-d60f-4a27-a2da-79b480332f33",
                                                "sense_id": "1720e38d-4a85-36ac-bd53-0f39d4c684b5",
                                                "text": "He swam the Esk river where ford there was none."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "382589ed-84e4-369c-8f64-0e2d13a8ce6a",
                                        "entry_id": "8003c089-83ad-3b87-a687-c807b7e55044",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stream; a current."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2680dc2-eb84-450d-909b-94b21468a227",
                                                "sense_id": "382589ed-84e4-369c-8f64-0e2d13a8ce6a",
                                                "text": "With water of the ford / Or of the clouds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0916259-3020-491a-b34f-31776c141764",
                                                "sense_id": "382589ed-84e4-369c-8f64-0e2d13a8ce6a",
                                                "text": "Permit my ghost to pass the Stygian ford."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ford",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1fba54db-7f3e-3cef-87d1-efd856177472",
                                        "entry_id": "7c79bc1f-3001-3dd7-a8dc-20ca205d3720",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cross a stream by walking through it."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07e2ed46-02e5-4f05-a411-b8cc2fc2adfc",
                                                "sense_id": "1fba54db-7f3e-3cef-87d1-efd856177472",
                                                "text": "He named that place, for it was near her dwelling, and on the road between Balerynie and Heriotside, which fords the Sker Burn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7bb304b-ba63-4599-b339-71ff1578b919",
                                                "sense_id": "1fba54db-7f3e-3cef-87d1-efd856177472",
                                                "text": "Since the time of Seyavi the deer have shifted their feeding ground across the valley at the beginning of deep snows, by way of the Black Rock, fording the river at Charley's Butte, and making straight for the mouth of the cañon that is the easiest going to the winter pastures on Waban."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5bd7b15-b8b4-4f26-a9d4-cc59d6483dd5",
                                                "sense_id": "1fba54db-7f3e-3cef-87d1-efd856177472",
                                                "text": "Ratau drove with reckless authority through the quiet morning fires of his father's and forefathers' town and forded a river of goats on the road leading out of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c6373b5-e100-47e9-8419-d80006ce1032",
                                                "sense_id": "1fba54db-7f3e-3cef-87d1-efd856177472",
                                                "text": "2016, Bruce McClure and Deborah Byrd, \"EarthSky's meteor shower guide for 2016\" in earthsky.org, http://earthsky.org/astronomy-essentials/earthskys-meteor-shower-guide\nSome who witnessed the 1966 Leonid meteor storm said they felt as if they needed to grip the ground, so strong was the impression of Earth plowing along through space, fording the meteoroid stream."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
